1
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:03,120
Maraud. Maraud.

2
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:06,940
Did you see everything?

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,230
Yeah.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,080
I see.

5
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:16,440
I broke my promise to go.

6
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,880
One more regret.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,020
Maraudöglich

8
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:28,920
I'm sorry! Dr.

9
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,010
Megimonose,

10
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:40,760
Here, give me your hand. What for?

11
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,120
Kuma entrusted this to me.

12
00:00:44,520 --> 00:00:47,167
It's a little present
for your 10th birthday.

13
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,740
Wait, it's from Dad? Really?

14
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,800
There you go.

15
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:56,140
A sapphire?

16
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,740
It's so pretty!

17
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,620
It looks like the sun!

18
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:01,660
Oh, I love it so much!

19
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:03,840
So that's what it is. Yep.

20
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:05,700
Like the sun god!

21
00:01:07,940 --> 00:01:10,293
Kuma just said it was a good luck charm.

22
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:12,952
Who could have imagined?

23
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:16,277
Kuma saw promise in
that boy two years ago,

24
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:19,140
and now he's turned into
something like this.

25
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:25,080
Speaking of, is it true Straw Hat
is my dad's best friend's son? Yes.

26
00:01:25,360 --> 00:01:28,337
I was surprised when you
two arrived here together.

27
00:01:28,420 --> 00:01:30,361
Fate can work in mysterious ways.

28
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,217
You've been in that room
for a while, you know.

29
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:37,182
You've missed out on quite a number
of happenings here on Egghead.

30
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:42,511
For example, Strawhead Luffy and his
crew just saved me from a deadly pinch.

31
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,500
I'll get you up to speed.

32
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:47,686
Then we'll join them
once you've rested a bit.

33
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,280
I truly am sorry, Bunny.

34
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:55,280
I'm just a paltry hired hand, after all.

35
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:56,970
No.

36
00:01:58,840 --> 00:01:59,670
No!

37
00:01:59,753 --> 00:02:00,940
This isn't your fault!

38
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,100
It's his!

39
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,400
Damn it!

40
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:22,717
I can't move at all!

41
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:24,212
What the hell did he do?

42
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:25,810
Honey!

43
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,357
How are we going to get out of this?

44
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,270
I don't know.

45
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,068
I've never seen this power.

46
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,060
Hungry food.

47
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:43,910
Meat.

48
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,400
Somebody get me meat.

49
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:50,840
I'm begging you.

50
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:53,937
I wish I could, but I can't move.

51
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,620
Reporting in.

52
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:59,460
Vegapunk's bodyguard,
Sentomaru, has been captured.

53
00:03:01,980 --> 00:03:03,040
Sentomaru.

54
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:06,170
Bonnie.

55
00:03:09,180 --> 00:03:12,840
Listen to me, pirate jewelry, Bonnie.

56
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,940
Your father, Bartholomew Kuma,

57
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,460
is dead.

58
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,317
What's going on in there?

59
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:29,106
No one below the rank of Commodore
can enter, so we don't know.

60
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:33,120
Have you seen today's news?

61
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:37,951
Apparently, the new Emperor of
the Sea just took a hostage.

62
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,280
Um, well, it's quite the bold move.

63
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,834
I'd wager some bloodshed is inevitable.

64
00:03:46,740 --> 00:03:50,277
It says the Navy sent more
battleships than they sent to Ohara.

65
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,357
Seems excessive.

66
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,220
I sure hope Dr.

67
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,438
Vegapunk is alright

68
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,117
You've got it all wrong.

69
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,437
Watch you silly billies!

70
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,940
Keep your hands up like this.

71
00:04:03,460 --> 00:04:04,660
And kablam!

72
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,780
There, you get it?

73
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:09,057
You're amazing.

74
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:11,720
One more time, I want to see it again!

75
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:15,037
No, I can't see it out of my pants.

76
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:16,797
You greedy boys and girls!

77
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,240
You're insatiable.

78
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,900
Is something wrong, dragon?

79
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:28,019
Let's say Kuma is being driven by
a fragment of his remaining psyche.

80
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:31,620
If you were him, where would you go, Eva?

81
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:33,210
Huh?

82
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:38,860
I'd march my cyborg butt straight
to Marie Joie and open fire.

83
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:43,000
But Kuma isn't like that.

84
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:45,500
It just leaves.

85
00:04:52,860 --> 00:04:54,520
But not to worry.

86
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:58,180
It's time to join your
father in the afterlife.

87
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:10,010
Fine!

88
00:05:10,220 --> 00:05:11,340
Then go ahead!

89
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:13,680
But you're coming with me!

90
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,360
Distorted future!

91
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:24,377
Nika, like...

92
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:26,720
Nika... Future!

93
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:43,980
What is this?

94
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:46,480
I got weaker again.

95
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,230
Why?

96
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,340
Of course.

97
00:05:51,840 --> 00:05:55,040
You are that fool's child.

98
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:06,960
But that is all you know, a name.

99
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:14,500
You have no idea what it is.

100
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,640
You know nothing.

101
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:25,080
What the hell are you
talking about, old man?

102
00:06:26,920 --> 00:06:30,180
It seems she truly is crudous.

103
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:34,020
She hasn't made the connection
between Nika and Straw Hat.

104
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:37,580
What a pity.

105
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,080
What are you doing?

106
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,960
Who gave Straw Hat all of that food?

107
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:49,280
Not us, sir.

108
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,237
We didn't give him anything, I swear.

109
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:53,860
Cuff him with Sea Prism Stone at once.

110
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,017
Of course, right away.

111
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:55,930
Yes, sir.

112
00:06:56,013 --> 00:06:56,980
Stop right there!

113
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,720
Go away!

114
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:08,920
What's happening?

115
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,920
I can't change his age.

116
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,080
But why?

117
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:16,740
You seem to be wondering
why your strength is waning.

118
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:18,890
Why?

119
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:21,800
Do you know where your power came from?

120
00:07:22,260 --> 00:07:24,457
It was given to you.

121
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,000
By me.

122
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,100
What?

123
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:38,100
It was an experiment.

124
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,280
You were given a Devil Fruit extract.

125
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:48,420
I wondered if an infant who could not
eat solid food could be granted power.

126
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:52,180
But the AJ's fruit is useless.

127
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:58,097
It allows you to transform into any
possible future version of yourself,

128
00:07:58,180 --> 00:07:59,440
but as you learn

129
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:05,080
to face reality, you begin to see
that your potential is quite narrow.

130
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:10,420
You want to believe that
Nika is real, don't you?

131
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,960
Nika is real!

132
00:08:12,340 --> 00:08:15,677
I've been searching for him ever
since you took my dad from me!

133
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:18,857
I knew if I found him, he'd
have the power to set dad free!

134
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:25,800
And yet, your weakening power is proof
that your faith in Nika is ebbing.

135
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:32,480
Your father also believed in
that foolish buccaneer legend.

136
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:35,860
I remember what he said
to me many years ago.

137
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:41,640
I want to be like Nika and
protect people from suffering.

138
00:08:44,320 --> 00:08:49,137
Before she died, your mother was the
eighth wife of someone from the Holy Land,

139
00:08:49,220 --> 00:08:52,440
and I conducted drug experiments on her.

140
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:58,000
But they were a failure, and
those blue blemishes appeared.

141
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:06,322
Disappointment aside, it was interesting
that her child inherited the side effects.

142
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,120
Hey, I think something fell from the sky.

143
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:30,280
It was you.

144
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:31,780
It was all you.

145
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,720
That's what happened to her.

146
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:38,180
It was your experiment!

147
00:09:39,540 --> 00:09:43,440
The sapphire scales took
Kuma's family apart!

148
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:48,320
He sacrificed himself to save
his daughter from that sickness,

149
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:52,840
and you acted like your deal
was a favor to him! Oh, no.

150
00:09:55,660 --> 00:09:58,780
You failed to see this
from my perspective.

151
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:05,180
Tell me, Doctor, do you concern yourself
with the feelings of mere insects?

152
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:13,320
I should think not.

153
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,020
Is that a pet the beast up? No.

154
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:31,340
Look closer.

155
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:34,180
He has paw pads on his hands.

156
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,460
It can't be!

157
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,740
It's the real Kuma!

158
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,580
This is an emergency!

159
00:10:54,060 --> 00:10:55,825
I'm on the southwestern shore!

160
00:10:55,940 --> 00:11:00,020
And the former warlord of the sea,
Bartholomew Kuma, has appeared!

161
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:02,817
He's advancing towards
the island's center!

162
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:04,841
The authority chip isn't working!

163
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:06,960
I have no way to stop it now!

164
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,440
Kuma's here? But bye!

165
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:22,080
What are you going on about, Kuma?

166
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:23,820
That's impossible.

167
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:27,730
I can't do it.

168
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:30,120
I'm too afraid.

169
00:11:33,160 --> 00:11:34,720
I can't say a word.

170
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:47,320
Stop him!

171
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,520
Open fire now! Yes, sir!

172
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:04,740
Hey, Dad.

173
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,720
I feel like I'm falling apart.

174
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:20,630
Maybe.

175
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:33,080
Maybe it would be easier

176
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,760
if I gave up and died right now.

177
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,360
I'm sorry. Dad!

178
00:13:03,420 --> 00:13:05,620
This is insufferable.

179
00:13:05,940 --> 00:13:08,160
Silence, you noisy brat.

180
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,720
Shoot her in the head.

181
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:19,140
Stop it!

182
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:41,440
I'm sorry, Dad.

183
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:46,860
You worked so hard to save my life.

184
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:13,700
Oh, my God. Dad!

185
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:16,670
Dad!

186
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:24,060
Put all of you, Kuma!

187
00:14:32,440 --> 00:14:33,880
I'm impossible.

188
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,980
Why is this happening, Vegapunk?

189
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:42,340
What did you do?

190
00:14:43,520 --> 00:14:45,120
This is absurd.

191
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,060
He's supposed to be dead.

192
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:51,840
Listen to me, buccaneer boy.

193
00:14:52,180 --> 00:14:55,000
You will live as a
slave, then you will die.

194
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:56,920
That is your lot in life.

195
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,540
Your mother's in heaven now.

196
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:05,400
But you know, it's better this way.

197
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,320
Kumachi, I'm so happy!

198
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:15,260
I'm sorry, Kumaji, but
I'm going to die soon.

199
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:33,620
Why is he still alive?

200
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:37,040
I killed him when the
revolutionaries took him.

201
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:42,020
He should have self-destructed already!

202
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,000
I pressed the switch myself!

203
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:30,480
C-Saturn, no!

204
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,580
Curse you!

205
00:16:38,840 --> 00:16:39,780
The city.

206
00:16:40,060 --> 00:16:42,420
Hey, what now? Do we stay put?

207
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:44,060
Did Kuma do all that?

208
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,800
He's done it now!

209
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,440
He backed one of the five elders!

210
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:55,680
What? No!

211
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,657
They're the highest
authority in the world!

212
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,858
He's lost his mind!

213
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:00,906
A slave just struck an elder.

214
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:02,480
This can't be happening!

215
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:04,840
It's completely unheard of!

216
00:17:12,160 --> 00:17:13,480
Rescue Saint Saturn!

217
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,445
He's buried underneath
the collapsed buildings!

218
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:18,720
I can move!

219
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:20,520
Hey, me too!

220
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:24,240
All thanks to Kuma, huh?
Hey, Bonnie! You okay?

221
00:17:27,620 --> 00:17:29,020
It's no time to lose!

222
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:31,966
Grab Bonnie and we can
head up to the sunning!

223
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,517
We don't have to win this fight!

224
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,071
We just have to get away!

225
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:39,279
I'll grab Comane, take him with us!

226
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,020
Wait a sec!

227
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,100
I don't know what happened.

228
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:58,300
I never installed that
self-destruct switch in you.

229
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:01,031
I feared that if I turned you into a bomb,

230
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:05,280
that the government would be tempted
to use you as a suicide weapon.

231
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,960
But I could only disobey them so much,

232
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:12,740
so I decided to install a
total shutdown switch instead.

233
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:18,220
Now that it has been pressed, you
should be in a vegetative state.

234
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:23,020
You shouldn't be able to respond to
commands, let alone act on your own.

235
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:26,860
If you don't possess
reason, what can you act on?

236
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:29,340
What drove you to Bonnie's side?

237
00:18:29,660 --> 00:18:31,480
Science cannot explain it.

238
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,140
It's illogical.

239
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:41,020
So the tales must be true, then.

240
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:45,559
It's not their physical strength
that makes Buccaneer people special.

241
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:48,400
At one point in time, they...

242
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:53,600
That's it.

243
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:54,920
It's over now.

244
00:18:58,320 --> 00:18:59,150
Kuma.

245
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,040
Any luck here?

246
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,080
No, Straw Hat just vanished on us.

247
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,800
What do we tell HQ?

248
00:19:13,900 --> 00:19:16,340
Thank you, Dad, for everything.

249
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:19,180
I saw your memories.

250
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,380
I saw your whole life.

251
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:24,540
And you know, you weren't
the only one I saw.

252
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,160
I saw Mom.

253
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,740
I'm so happy. I love her.

254
00:19:29,060 --> 00:19:29,917
She was the best.

255
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,720
And thank you for writing
me so many letters.

256
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,280
Reading those words made me so happy.

257
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:43,037
It's not fair.

258
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:45,257
Everybody says that you're a tyrant.

259
00:19:45,340 --> 00:19:47,957
But I know you're the nicest person ever.

260
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,417
And the coolest.

261
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:51,780
I have the best dad in the world.

262
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:55,397
Believe me.

263
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:57,420
I'll never forget it.

264
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:27,300
He's coming back!

265
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:28,980
Dammit, this is bad!

266
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:31,044
One punch ain't taking him out!

267
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,280
Speak, Vegapunk.

268
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:05,117
What is your explanation for this?

269
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,120
Was it your doing?

270
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,997
Well, I suppose it must look that way.

271
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:15,880
You could say it was the
power of love, if you like.

272
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:17,757
Very well, then.

273
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:20,640
Call it one of humanity's delusions.

274
00:21:20,760 --> 00:21:23,300
An error in their construction.

275
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:32,980
Hey, what just happened?

276
00:21:33,120 --> 00:21:35,002
It looks like he's regenerating.

277
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:35,950
Farewell.

278
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:38,780
I have no more use for you.

279
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:39,820
Get away, Dad!

280
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:41,280
Get out of there!

281
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:45,440
Leave Bonnie alone, you spider geezer!

282
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:47,300
Get the hell out of here!

283
00:21:49,940 --> 00:21:51,600
Come with sin, our asses!

284
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,053
We got a debt to repay!

285
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,660
Ready to go?

286
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,250
You were right.

287
00:21:58,333 --> 00:22:00,900
You aren't the same crew I faced before.

288
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:10,820
I've gone back to hell already!

289
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:17,360
Why don't you show me? Flanky!

290
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:20,220
How much you've implied!

291
00:22:26,180 --> 00:22:29,100
VEGAPUNK, MY DAD ISN'T MOVING! KUMA?

292
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,440
WHAT DO WE DO?

293
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:33,460
Atlas, CARRY HIM TO THE LAMO PHASE!

294
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,520
EASY Pass, I GOT THIS!

295
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:40,160
QUICKLY, Atlas!

296
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:46,620
LEAVE THIS ONE TO ME!

297
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,967
TAKE CARE OF Brain AND KUMA!

298
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,720
We're just gonna let him escape.

299
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:00,900
I don't care.

300
00:23:04,140 --> 00:23:05,457
This is a mess.

301
00:23:05,540 --> 00:23:07,857
Now we've got Kuma here too.

302
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:10,577
That's too many big
shots all in one place.

303
00:23:10,660 --> 00:23:12,960
Better get this over with quick.

304
00:23:13,640 --> 00:23:15,540
Now you can't take the pressure?

305
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:20,740
What a sad man you've become, Kizaru
That's not Zoborcelino I knew.

306
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:23,860
I am pathetic, aren't I?

307
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:30,500
If I'd known today would be like this, I
would have wanted a darker pair of shades.

308
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:33,557
This is an order.

309
00:23:33,640 --> 00:23:36,020
Eliminate all enemies of the government.

310
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:38,300
Let none of them remain.

311
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:42,180
Prepare all ships for the Buster Call!

312
00:23:42,520 --> 00:23:46,520
This island has been designated as
a threat to the world government.

313
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:49,520
All units, prepare for bombardment!

314
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:53,674
In the name of justice, we'll
burn it all to the ground!

315
00:23:53,940 --> 00:23:55,160
Spare no effort!

316
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:56,660
Show no mercy!

317
00:23:57,040 --> 00:23:59,820
Open fire and leave nothing behind!

318
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,270
Fate!

319
00:24:02,353 --> 00:24:03,820
Deadly's a master call!

320
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:08,380
Those who study the forbidden
secrets of the world.

321
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:11,020
Those who carry traitor's blood.

322
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:15,060
Those who awaken the
might of an ancient god.

323
00:24:18,900 --> 00:24:24,960
All inconveniences,
all must be eradicated.

324
00:24:47,700 --> 00:24:50,500
Thank you.
